Write a js code block to build a pyramid in minecraft using sandstone, the pyramid should be large and centered just like a real pyramid.

examples.frozen_answer:
```js
const size = 15; // Total height (layers), width, and depth for a square base pyramid
const center = Math.floor(size / 2);

// Build the pyramid layers from top (1 block) to bottom (largest layer)
for (let layer = 0; layer < size; layer++) {
    const height = layer + 1; // Number of blocks in each dimension for this layer
    const half = Math.floor((height - 1) / 2);
    // Loop over x, y, z coordinates relative to center
    for (let dx = -half; dx <= half; dx++) {
        const x = center + dx;
        for (let dy = -half; dy <= half; dy++) {
            const y = center + dy;
            for (let dz = -half; dz <= half; dz++) {
                // Only keep points within the diamond cross-section of the pyramid
                if (
                    Math.abs(dx) + Math.abs(dy) + Math.abs(dz) <= half
                ) {
                    const z = center + dz;
                    // For sandstone, use z as vertical (height) to stack upwards
                    // Adjust coordinate system if needed (swap y and z for Minecraft's orientation)
                    await skills.placeBlock(bot, 'sandstone', x, y + layer, z);
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```
